{"name":"Partridge Grey","hex":"#919098","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"partridge","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any bird of a number of genera in the family Phasianidae, notably in the genera Perdix and Alectoris.","The flesh or meat of this bird eaten as food."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/partridge"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Partridge","blocks":[{"text":"A partridge is a medium-sized galliform bird in any of several genera, with a wide native distribution throughout parts of Europe, Asia and Africa. Several species have been introduced to the Americas. They are sometimes grouped in the Perdicinae subfamily of the Phasianidae. However, molecular research suggests that partridges are not a distinct taxon within the superfamily Phasianoidea, but that some species are closer to the pheasants, while others are closer to the junglefowl."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/CRESTED_WOOD-PARTRIDGE_%287181284331%29.jpg/330px-CRESTED_WOOD-PARTRIDGE_%287181284331%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Partridge","wikidata":"Q732775"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.or